CORE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY ("CONVERGENCE MODEL")
===============================================================================

Traditional simulation systems assume:
    local correctness → eventual consistency

DVSM inverts this:

    deterministic execution → global verification → accepted reality

Thus:

    computation is not "trusted"
    computation is "verified"

===============================================================================
DESIGN DECISIONS (LONG-STANDING TRADEOFF RESOLUTION)
===============================================================================

1. HASH AS TRUTH ANCHOR (S_ECHO MODEL)
------------------------------------------------
Decision:
    Use a deterministic hash as canonical state identity.

Rationale:
    Enables cross-node verification without full state transfer.

Tradeoff:
    Rejects floating-point equivalence models due to drift risk.

2. NO FLOATING POINT SIMULATION
------------------------------------------------
Decision:
    Fixed-point arithmetic only (Q32.32 model).

Rationale:
    Ensures identical results across CPU/GPU/WASM.

3. SNAPSHOT + ROLLBACK OVER REPLAY GUESSING
------------------------------------------------
Decision:
    Store deterministic snapshots rather than reconstructive replay.

Rationale:
    Prevents divergence accumulation over long simulation chains.

4. CONSENSUS OVER LOCAL AUTHORITY
------------------------------------------------
Decision:
    State validity requires quorum agreement.

Rationale:
    Prevents single-node authoritative corruption.

5. DETERMINISTIC ECS (STRUCT OF ARRAYS)
------------------------------------------------
Decision:
    No HashMap-based ECS indexing.

Rationale:
    Eliminates nondeterministic iteration ordering.

===============================================================================
MATHEMATICAL MODEL
===============================================================================

STATE EVOLUTION:

    S_{t+1} = Ξ(S_t, I_t)

STATE IDENTITY:

    H_t = S_ECHO(S_t)

CONSENSUS FUNCTION:

    C(H_t) → {FINAL, FORK, VOID, DRIFT}

FINALITY RULE:

    FINAL ⇔ quorum(H_t)

===============================================================================
INVARIANTS
===============================================================================

I1. Determinism:
    identical input → identical state everywhere

I2. Temporal Discreteness:
    time is tick-based, not continuous

I3. Hash Sovereignty:
    all state identity is derived from S_ECHO

I4. No Silent Divergence:
    all inconsistencies manifest as rollback or fork

I5. No Partial Truth:
    state is either accepted or rejected globally

