===============================================================================
DVSM :: MISSING LOGIC ADDENDUM
"FORMAL COMPLETENESS + EXECUTION CLOSURE LAYER"
===============================================================================

PURPOSE:
This section defines the missing formal components required to make the
DVSM specification computationally complete, including:

- causal completeness of Ξ
- deterministic ordering guarantees
- consensus liveness constraints
- rollback correctness bounds
- state-space closure properties
- execution termination semantics

===============================================================================
1. CAUSAL COMPLETENESS OF Ξ
===============================================================================

The system assumes:

    S_{t+1} = Ξ(S_t, I_t)

MISSING CONSTRAINT:

Ξ must be:

    (C1) Pure function
    (C2) Total over state space
    (C3) Order-preserving over command reduction
    (C4) Side-effect free

FORMAL DEFINITION:

    ∀ S, I:
        Ξ(S, I) is defined
        Ξ(S, I) produces exactly one S'

IMPLICATION:

No undefined state transitions exist.
No partial execution states are valid.

===============================================================================
2. DETERMINISTIC ORDERING INVARIANT (DOI)
===============================================================================

MISSING RULE:

Command application order MUST be canonical.

Define:

    O(cmds) = deterministic ordering function

Requirement:

    Ξ(S, I) = fold(O(I), S)

Where O is:

    - stable across platforms
    - independent of memory layout
    - independent of thread scheduling

WITHOUT THIS:
S_ECHO becomes non-portable.

===============================================================================
3. STATE SPACE CLOSURE PROPERTY
===============================================================================

MISSING AXIOM:

The system state space is closed under Ξ.

FORMALLY:

    Ξ(S_t, I_t) ∈ 𝒮

Where:

    𝒮 = valid ECS state space

IMPLICATION:

No external mutation can produce invalid state.

All invalid states are unreachable by construction.

===============================================================================
4. CONSENSUS LIVENESS CONDITION
===============================================================================

Existing spec defines safety (no false acceptance),
but does NOT define liveness.

MISSING PROPERTY:

    If network is eventually synchronous,
    consensus must eventually terminate.

FORMALIZATION:

    ∃ T such that:
        ∀ t > T:
            C(H_t) = FINAL or VOID

IMPLICATION:

System cannot remain in indefinite DRIFT state.

===============================================================================
5. ROLLBACK CORRECTNESS BOUND
===============================================================================

MISSING RULE:

Rollback must preserve deterministic equivalence class.

Define equivalence:

    S_a ≡ S_b ⇔ S_ECHO(S_a) == S_ECHO(S_b)

ROLLBACK CONSTRAINT:

    restore(S_t) MUST satisfy:
        S_restored ≡ S_reference

IMPLICATION:

Rollback is not approximate recovery.
It is exact state equivalence restoration.

===============================================================================
6. TEMPORAL CAUSALITY CONSTRAINT
===============================================================================

MISSING AXIOM:

No future state may influence past computation.

FORMALLY:

    S_t depends only on:
        S_{t-1}, I_t

NOT:

    S_{t+k}

IMPLICATION:

Prevents speculative execution leakage into truth layer.

===============================================================================
7. HASH CONSISTENCY BINDING RULE (S_ECHO STRICTNESS)
===============================================================================

MISSING PROPERTY:

S_ECHO must be:

    injective over reachable state space (practically collision-resistant)

FORMAL RULE:

    S_ECHO(S_a) = S_ECHO(S_b)
        ⇒ S_a ≡ S_b   (system assumption)

IMPLICATION:

Hash is not metadata.
Hash IS identity.

===============================================================================
8. FAILURE DETERMINISM MODEL
===============================================================================

MISSING CLASSIFICATION:

All failures MUST map into deterministic categories:

    F1: INVALID_INPUT
    F2: CONSENSUS_FORK
    F3: STATE_DRIFT
    F4: ROLLBACK_LIMIT_REACHED

RULE:

No undefined failure states exist.

EVERY failure is classifiable.

===============================================================================
9. EXECUTION TERMINATION SEMANTICS
===============================================================================

MISSING RULE:

System MUST define termination conditions:

Termination occurs when:

    (A) tick >= MAX_TICKS
    (B) consensus = VOID permanently
    (C) rollback buffer exhausted
    (D) external shutdown signal

FORMAL:

    TERMINATE ⇔ ∃ condition above

IMPLICATION:

No infinite undefined runtime state.

===============================================================================
10. OBSERVABILITY COMPLETENESS PRINCIPLE
===============================================================================

MISSING AXIOM:

Every state transition must be observable via:

    H_t = S_ECHO(S_t)

IMPLICATION:

No hidden state evolution exists.

System is fully auditable at hash level.

===============================================================================
11. FINAL COMPLETENESS THEOREM (CLOSURE)
===============================================================================

If all conditions hold:

- Ξ is pure and total
- O(cmds) is deterministic
- S_ECHO is stable and injective
- consensus is live under synchrony
- rollback preserves equivalence classes
- state space is closed

THEN:

    DVSM defines a complete deterministic transition system:

        𝒮 × 𝕀 → 𝒮

WITH:

    globally verifiable state identity
    deterministic replay equivalence
    consensus-bound finality
